// REMOVAL IS FREE HERE, BECAUSE THE TYPED REPLACEMENT ALREADY EXISTS AND ALREADY WINS.
// The honest traffic never used this arm: `all_callee_keys_registry_or_bridge_total`
// consults the TyCtxt-anchored registry FIRST (trust_verify.rs:18569) and only then the
// string lane (:18575), and the registry's `Range` test is a real `TyKind` test —
// `"Range" => def_path_has_module_segment(tcx, did, "range") && inner(0)
// .is_some_and(|t| matches!(t.kind(), ty::Int(_) | ty::Uint(_)))`, trust_verify.rs:27410.
// MEASURED on the same driver, honest fixtures:
//
//     [PF_ZEROGATE] fn=H::honest_range_next  arm=registry callee=<…Range<u64> as …Iterator>::next
//     [PF_ZEROGATE] fn=H::honest_range_usize arm=registry callee=<…Range<usize> as …Iterator>::next
//     [PF_ZEROGATE] fn=H::honest_for_loop    arm=registry callee=<…Range<usize> as …IntoIterator>::into_iter
