                // whose body lives in `core` (so `resolve_call_target` would abort the
                // whole function here, BEFORE the `StepBy::next` yield-bound logic above is
                // ever reached). The constructor is TOTAL — it only wraps the inner
                // iterator. Model its result (the `StepBy` value) as a fresh OPAQUE `Undef`
                // and continue, exactly like `total_range_iterator_call`'s `into_iter` arm.
                // SOUNDNESS: this asserts NOTHING about the `StepBy` — the `[start, end)`
                // yield bound `start <= v < end` is emitted SEPARATELY by the
                // `total_iterator_step_by_next` arm (above) when `next()` is later called on
                // this `StepBy`. So the constructor modeling is a pure unblock (no fact),
